<!--
  Runtime directives for the Native AOT compiler (ILC).

  Shipped inside the package (buildTransitive) and applied automatically by
  Bielu.AspNetCore.AsyncApi.targets, because without it *every* consumer publishing Native AOT hits
  the failure below — it is a property of our ByteBard.AsyncAPI dependency, not of their code.

  ByteBard.AsyncAPI resolves enums from their display names reflectively:

      ByteBard.AsyncAPI.Writers.StringExtensions.GetEnumFromDisplayName<T>(string)
        -> Enum.GetValues()
        -> Array.CreateInstance(typeof(TEnum), n)

  Without this the app publishes and starts, then throws on the first document request:

      System.NotSupportedException: 'ByteBard.AsyncAPI.Models.ReferenceType[]' is missing native
      code or metadata.

  Two separate things are needed, which is the part worth remembering:

  1. `<Assembly Dynamic="Required All">` keeps metadata for the assembly's own types.
  2. Each **array** type has to be named on its own. An array is a constructed type that ILC only
     emits when it can see it being used, and `Array.CreateInstance(type, n)` is invisible to it.
     Rooting the assembly alone is NOT enough — that was verified: the failure survived it, and it
     survived `TrimmerRootAssembly` too, which governs trimming rather than metadata generation.

  Every enum in the assembly is listed rather than just the one that happened to fail first, because
  `GetEnumFromDisplayName<T>` is generic and any of them can reach it depending on the document being
  written. The list is small and the assembly is a pinned dependency, so it is cheap to keep exact.

  The `<Type>` entries must be nested inside `<Assembly>`; ILC rejects them as a direct child of
  `<Application>` with `"Type" is not a supported Runtime Directive`.

  Revisit if ByteBard.AsyncAPI ever becomes trim/AOT-annotated; it currently publishes IL2104/IL3053
  from its own assembly.
-->
<Directives xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/netfx/2013/01/metadata">
  <Application>
    <Assembly Name="ByteBard.AsyncAPI" Dynamic="Required All">
      <Type Name="ByteBard.AsyncAPI.AsyncApiVersion[]" Dynamic="Required All" />
      <Type Name="ByteBard.AsyncAPI.Models.AsyncApiAction[]" Dynamic="Required All" />
      <Type Name="ByteBard.AsyncAPI.Models.AsyncApiFormat[]" Dynamic="Required All" />
      <Type Name="ByteBard.AsyncAPI.Models.Avro.LogicalTypes.LogicalType[]" Dynamic="Required All" />
      <Type Name="ByteBard.AsyncAPI.Models.AvroFieldOrder[]" Dynamic="Required All" />
      <Type Name="ByteBard.AsyncAPI.Models.AvroPrimitiveType[]" Dynamic="Required All" />
      <Type Name="ByteBard.AsyncAPI.Models.ParameterLocation[]" Dynamic="Required All" />
      <Type Name="ByteBard.AsyncAPI.Models.ReferenceType[]" Dynamic="Required All" />
      <Type Name="ByteBard.AsyncAPI.Models.SchemaType[]" Dynamic="Required All" />
      <Type Name="ByteBard.AsyncAPI.Models.SecuritySchemeType[]" Dynamic="Required All" />
      <Type Name="ByteBard.AsyncAPI.Writers.ReferenceInlineSetting[]" Dynamic="Required All" />
      <Type Name="ByteBard.AsyncAPI.Writers.ScopeType[]" Dynamic="Required All" />
    </Assembly>
  </Application>
</Directives>
